{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "x-touch-extender",
  "name": "Behringer X-Touch Extender",
  "notes": "Behringer X-Touch Extender in Mackie Control / 'Mackie Control XT' mode (set via the config menu: hold CH1 SELECT while powering on, encoder 1 = MC). Modelled deliberately as MC, NOT the manual's 'Ctrl' mode: only MC gives motorized pitchbend faders and the Mackie scribble-strip sysex the app supports, and it makes the addressing identical to the X-Touch base's first 8 channel strips — a true extension. Per strip index n (0-7): V-Pot encoder on CC 16+n, its LED ring on CC 48+n (values 32=off..43=full), the encoder push button on Note 32+n (no LED). Rec/Solo/Mute/Select on Notes 0+n / 8+n / 16+n / 24+n. Faders are pitchbend on channels 1-8, motorized. Scribble strips are addressed by slot index via the shared Mackie sysex (2 lines of 7 chars). The Extender has no master fader, transport, function or master section. Channel meters (CC 90-97 in Ctrl mode) are not represented — v1 never supported meters. Scribble-strip and LED feedback still need verification on real Extender hardware.",
  "manufacturer": "Behringer",
  "mode": "mc",
  "defaultMidiChannel": 1,
  "layout": {
    "width": 16,
    "height": 18.5
  },
